WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.069
-My first guests are
a Grammy-nominated

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:06.806
and multi-platinum selling group
you can see in the new special

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:10.343
on NBC, "Olympic Dreams
Featuring Jonas Brothers,"

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:12.979
which airs tomorrow night
at 8:00 p.m.

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:15.281
Here are the Jonas Brothers!

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:17.150
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.851
That's what I'm talking about!

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:20.587
-Why, hello.
-Oh, that's my man!

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.589
That is my -- Look at that.

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:24.757
I don't pick favorites,
but come on.

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:26.425
That's what I'm talking about
right there.

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:28.060
Tonight Dough, my man.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:30.030
Welcome back.
-Oh, me? Sorry.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.564
-Thank you all
for being on the show.

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:34.167
I miss talking to you guys.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.468
I want to talk about
the new special.

00:00:36.468 --> 00:00:38.104
I want to talk about new music.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:40.840
I want to talk about
going back on tour.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.942
There's a lot to talk about
and discuss.

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:44.277
Let's talk about the tour.

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:47.413
Are you excited to be back?

00:00:47.413 --> 00:00:49.048
-Incredibly excited.
-Couldn't be more excited.

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:50.116
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.116 --> 00:00:53.586
You know, it's been a long year.

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:56.623
But a year and a half of
craziness and, you know,

00:00:56.623 --> 00:01:01.261
the fact that we were basically
one of the last tours to go out

00:01:01.261 --> 00:01:06.298
pre-COVID, and we'll be one of
the first ones back outdoors

00:01:06.298 --> 00:01:09.802
in front of our fans again is
just gonna be a dream come true

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:12.304
after what's been a wild ride.

00:01:12.304 --> 00:01:14.907
Hope to see you at a show
if you can make it out to one.

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:17.176
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah. I've been to one.

00:01:17.176 --> 00:01:18.578
-Oh, yeah.

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.680
-Going on tour, I mean,
are you a little rusty?

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.383
Do you remember anything?
Let me just pick a brother.

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:26.653
Joe, you tell me
an instance of some time

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:29.589
things didn't go as planned.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:32.292
-Yes, you know, things are out
of your control,

00:01:32.292 --> 00:01:35.528
and it's big stage,
lots of lights.

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:36.963
You never know
what's going to happen.

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:43.369
And on my birthday, we had
this big sign that said "JB's,"

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:46.438
standing for Justin Bieber,
that we were borrowing from him

00:01:46.438 --> 00:01:47.773
for us as Jonas Brothers.
-Yeah. Okay, okay, of course.

00:01:47.773 --> 00:01:50.209
Well, yeah, you have to
recycle and reuse. Why not?

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:51.710
-Yeah, yeah, of course.

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:54.080
And it lights up on fire.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.249
Well, it was one of
our first times using it.

00:01:56.249 --> 00:02:00.586
And this was at Woodstock,
and the fire alarm goes off,

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:04.423
and sprinklers just start
pouring on us on stage.

00:02:04.423 --> 00:02:08.261
So we're almost in a flood now
and the audience has to leave

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:09.662
before we can
even make the encore.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:12.131
But for me, selfishly,
we got to my after party

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:13.966
for my birthday quicker,
but I felt bad

00:02:13.966 --> 00:02:16.802
about not finishing the gig.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.802 --> 00:02:20.039
-Kevin, I saw this video
of your daughters

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:25.077
doing their best impression
of you guys, of Jonas Brothers.

00:02:25.077 --> 00:02:27.346
How do they see you?

00:02:27.346 --> 00:02:29.182
Do they see you
as uncles and dads

00:02:29.182 --> 00:02:32.018
or do they know you from TV?

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:35.154
-No, no. They see us
as the people they saw

00:02:35.154 --> 00:02:38.090
on "Hannah Montana" in that
one episode we did with her.

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:39.359
-Interesting.

00:02:39.359 --> 00:02:41.360
-They're completely obsessed
with that show now,

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:45.531
and they think we're
those people every day.

00:02:45.531 --> 00:02:48.234
-Yeah, I want to show a video of

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.835
your daughters
impersonating you guys.

00:02:49.835 --> 00:02:51.904
Here's Kevin's daughters.
Check this out. Cute.

00:02:51.904 --> 00:02:54.873
-I'm Nick.
-I'm Joe.

00:02:54.873 --> 00:02:57.010
-I'm Kevin.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:59.278
-I'm Kevin.

00:02:59.278 --> 00:03:00.479
-No, I'm Kevin.

00:03:00.479 --> 00:03:02.048
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:04.550
-Everybody wants to be Kevin.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.519
-Yeah, everybody wants to be
Kevin, yeah.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:10.056
-Yeah, she did say that
Nick is the funniest

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:12.758
when his hair is puffy,
so bringing it back

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:14.626
to that "Hannah Montana" days.

00:03:14.626 --> 00:03:16.562
-It's getting puffy once again.

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:18.764
It's growing out here,
so she can be real happy.

00:03:18.764 --> 00:03:20.399
-Yeah, exactly, bud.

00:03:20.399 --> 00:03:22.034
You guys have a memoir
coming out,

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:25.204
by the way, entitled "Blood."

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:28.240
Obviously because you're family.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.943
-We wrote it with blood.

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:32.445
-No, actually,
that's not the reason.

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:35.581
We're going to take a note out
of all the YouTubers

00:03:35.581 --> 00:03:38.184
that are having
these boxing matches.

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:40.586
We're going to have
a big UFC match.

00:03:40.586 --> 00:03:42.822
It's gonna be us vs.
the Hemsworth brothers.

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:44.790
-Oh, my God! Oh, no!

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:48.360
Don't do it!
Don't do it, please!

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:51.330
-The Hemsworths haven't e-mailed
us back yet.

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:52.999
but I think it's gonna be big.

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:55.401
-Yeah, maybe there's a couple of
Hemsworths out there

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:56.936
that we don't know of
that you can maybe

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.438
challenge or something.

00:03:58.438 --> 00:04:00.172
-A little bit closer
to our height as well.

00:04:00.172 --> 00:04:01.540
-Exactly, yeah.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:02.809
Well, congrats on that.

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:07.413
And I want to talk about
your show, "Olympic Dreams."

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:09.682
Kevin, can you set this up?

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:12.285
-Yeah, the show,
we're really excited about.

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:13.786
We got the opportunity
to pretend like

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:16.022
we're Olympic athletes
for a week or so.

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:19.359
And about a day of training
with some incredible athletes

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:21.661
and then actually compete
against each other.

00:04:21.661 --> 00:04:25.230
And they filmed it
for the audience at home

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:28.734
to watch and laugh at us.
It's been great so far.

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:32.538
-Nick, you broke a rib
doing this.

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:35.842
Are you okay now
and what happened?

00:04:35.842 --> 00:04:38.878
-I am, you know, now I think,
seven, eight weeks

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:40.613
removed from the injury.

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:43.983
I'm doing a lot better.
Nearly 100%.

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.651
It's not all that exciting.

00:04:45.651 --> 00:04:47.553
I mean, it's going to be
in the show,

00:04:47.553 --> 00:04:49.856
which people should watch
tomorrow night.

00:04:49.856 --> 00:04:52.991
But basically, you know,
we trained with

00:04:52.991 --> 00:04:55.628
real Olympic athletes
who have been doing this since

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:57.597
they were probably
four or five years old.

00:04:57.597 --> 00:05:00.866
And so, when they said to us,
"Yo, this is easy.

00:05:00.866 --> 00:05:04.370
You're gonna do the BMX track
that 11-year-olds do."

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.071
We thought, "We got this."

00:05:06.071 --> 00:05:07.940
What they didn't tell us
is that these 11-year-olds

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:10.242
have been doing it since
they were 3 or 4 years old.

00:05:10.242 --> 00:05:13.345
So cut to the three of us
trying to do that,

00:05:13.345 --> 00:05:16.548
and, you know, I took a spill,

00:05:16.548 --> 00:05:20.019
one of two spills
I took on the show,

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:22.088
and broke my rib.

00:05:22.088 --> 00:05:24.290
-Kevin's laughing, by the way.

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:25.924
-It was great.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:25.924 --> 00:05:27.660
-It couldn't have been
worse timing

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.096
because that week following,

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:32.131
we shot the music video
for our song with Marshmello,

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:33.532
"Leave Before You Love Me."

00:05:33.532 --> 00:05:35.968
I was hosting
the Billboard Music Awards

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:37.536
and performing with the brothers

00:05:37.536 --> 00:05:40.339
and we had "The Voice" finale
all in the same week of my --

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:42.408
[ Laughter ]
-We get it, Nick, you're famous.

00:05:42.408 --> 00:05:43.843
We get it, Nick, you're famous.
Geez.

00:05:43.843 --> 00:05:49.582
[ Laughter ]

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:50.983
-You guys are the greatest.

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:52.518
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:54.386
Here are Nick, Kevin
and Joe Jonas

00:05:54.386 --> 00:05:56.689
in "Olympic Dreams
Featuring Jonas Brothers."

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:58.724
It's gonna air tomorrow night
at 8:00 p.m. on NBC.

00:05:58.724 --> 00:06:00.092
Take a look.

00:06:00.092 --> 00:06:03.495
-Run through the hurdles,
don't slow down, and jump, okay?

00:06:03.495 --> 00:06:04.864
-Hey!
-Okay. Okay.

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:08.100
-You got some height, Nick.
-Not too bad.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.468
-Yes.
-Okay.

00:06:09.468 --> 00:06:12.305
-That was beautiful form, Kev.
-That was beautiful.

00:06:12.305 --> 00:06:13.972
-Staying low through those --
-Hey, how's it going, bros?

00:06:13.972 --> 00:06:15.541
Good to see you.
-Trying to stay --

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.776
Right, you're supposed to stay
through the power though, right?

00:06:17.776 --> 00:06:19.378
-You were.
-Am I doing that?

00:06:19.378 --> 00:06:21.046
-Better, but still --
I think you're still --

00:06:21.046 --> 00:06:22.781
-No, it's not better.

00:06:22.781 --> 00:06:23.849
Is it better than them
is the question.

00:06:23.849 --> 00:06:25.017
-Kevin needs
a lot of motivation.

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:26.118
-Kevin's already out here
fishing for compliments.

00:06:26.118 --> 00:06:28.754
-I need to know I'm doing okay!

00:06:28.754 --> 00:06:29.955
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:29.955 --> 00:06:31.757
-I'm Kevin. I'm Kevin.

00:06:31.757 --> 00:06:33.092
-I'm Kevin!

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:34.627
-Jonas Brothers, everybody!

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:36.695
"Olympic Dreams
Featuring Jonas Brothers"

00:06:36.695 --> 00:06:40.733
airs tomorrow at 8:00 p.m.
on NBC.

